# CS 255 – Business Requirements Document (Part One)

This repository contains **Part One** of the Business Requirements Document (BRD) for the DriverPass system, completed for *CS 255: System Analysis and Design* at Southern New Hampshire University.

Part One focuses on establishing the foundational understanding of the system by defining its purpose, background, and measurable objectives based on the client interview.

## 📌 Project Scope (Part One Only)

### **1. Purpose**
Defines the overall intent of the DriverPass system and what the client wants the system to accomplish.  
This section summarizes DriverPass’s goals to provide online classes, practice tests, and scheduling for driving lessons through a secure, web‑based platform.

### **2. System Background**
Explains the problem DriverPass aims to solve—high DMV test failure rates—and how the system will support improved driver training.  
This section outlines the major system components needed, including online learning, scheduling, tracking, and DMV integration.

### **3. Objectives and Goals**
Breaks down the system’s required capabilities into measurable, testable tasks.  
This includes account management, scheduling, reporting, role‑based access, DMV updates, and cross‑device accessibility.

## 🧩 Source Material
All requirements in Part One are derived from the **DriverPass Interview Transcript**, which details:
- Client expectations  
- User roles (Owner, IT Officer, Secretary, Customers)  
- Scheduling and training package structure  
- Security and tracking needs  
- Desired system flexibility and cloud hosting  

## 🎯 Purpose of This Submission
Part One establishes the foundation for:
- Functional and nonfunctional requirements  
- Use case diagrams  
- Activity diagrams  
- Class diagrams  
- Interface design (Part Two)  

It ensures the system design aligns with the client’s needs before moving into modeling and implementation planning.

